  "evidence": "TEXT_D: EU final-deal referendum with option to remain; seek close EU ties (single market/customs union access), Erasmus+, Europol/EAW; retain Human Rights Act and ECHR; roll back bulk surveillance and protect encryption; decriminalise drug possession and regulate cannabis; expand safe asylum routes (50,000 resettlements, protections for LGBT claimants), allow work after 6 months, remove students from migration stats; ambitious green agenda (60% renewables by 2030, oppose fracking, diesel phaseout); votes at 16 and proportional representation. TEXT_C: Regain full lawmaking supremacy outside ECJ/ECHR; exit single market/customs union with no “divorce” payment; near‑zero net migration target with five‑year moratorium on low‑skilled visas and benefits/NHS restrictions; ban face coverings in public; restore stop‑and‑search, add 20,000 police, tougher prisons; reduce foreign aid to 0.2% GNI; repeal Climate Change Act and leave Paris Agreement; promote shale and protect diesel owners; UK Bill of Rights and opt‑out of EAW.",
